From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:09:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Print the rated game report after a replay's result

A replay now also prints REPLAY_REPORT, the game report the lobby client
sends the rating bot at the end of a match, so a dedicated server can send
it on a player's behalf. It is built by the session's own
LobbyRatingReporter, loaded unchanged into a script interface next to the
simulation's, with the few engine calls it makes answered from the final
state. playerID is left out: the report is the same for every player but
for it, and the server fills it in for the player it reports for.

The conversion of the report into stanza attributes, renames included,
moves from XmppClient into GameReportAttributes.h, header-only and free of
gloox, so the replay produces exactly the attributes the lobby client
sends without linking the lobby.
